                <pb facs="0328" n="232" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">438.00/130: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Jordan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-24T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Your 2, January 13, 11 a.m., Department’s 424, August 8, 1921, your 537,
                    September 8, 1921.</p>
                <p>You will state informally to the Minister for Foreign Affairs that the suggestion
                    of his Government to the French Minister, communicated to the Department at the
                    latter’s request, is not acceptable to this Government, in view of the
                    assumption in the suggestion that the matter of the organization of the Claims
                    Commission is not governed by the Protocol of October 3, 1919. You may advise
                    the French Minister of this instruction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
